## Important: concurrent modification during the investigation

The working tree was being edited and committed by **another actor while I was running**. Timeline:

- Baseline when I started: `3dd6b29`, one pre-existing modification (`scripts/smoke-workflow-compat.mjs`).
- Mid-run: HEAD advanced to `2b0263e`, and 5 Phase 4 source files became modified — `workflow-engine-config.ts`, `workflow-engine-config.test.ts`, `workflow-engine.ts`, `workflow-files.test.ts`, `workflow-requirements-win.lock`.
- Late: HEAD advanced again to `518e19d` ("Probe workflow export rename semantics on each platform").

The diffs are substantive Phase 4 feature work (adding `extensions`/`extraPathsConfig` paths, `--extra-model-paths-config`/`--enable-manager` flags, XDG/HOME redirect env vars) — not anything a read-only test run would produce.

Because of this I **re-ran all five commands against the settled tree** and they all pass again. But any attestation of "which commit is green" is inherently racy here: HEAD moved twice under me.

## Tooling status

- **`codebase-memory-mcp`: connected.** Snapshot `G-Hyper-Studio-hyper-studio`, status `ready`, 631,399 nodes / 891,823 edges.
- **Snapshot is stale for Phase 4.** Despite reporting `head_sha == 3dd6b29`, it indexes **zero** nodes for `apps/desktop/electron/workflow-*` and `provider-jobs/*`. `search_graph` for `workflowRuntimeTarget` and `prepareWorkflowPaths` returned 0 results; `search_code` grep for `workflowRuntimeTarget` returned 0 matches while a control (`isAllowedExternalUrl`) matched 3 files. So the recorded SHA is not a reliable freshness signal — the index predates the Phase 4 files. **Graph-based discovery was useless for this phase; all findings come from the filesystem and test output.**
- **`graft`: connected and useful.** `.tools/graft/node_modules/.bin/graft.cmd map --max-dirs 12` ran fine and reported `apps/desktop/electron/ 87 files · 404 symbols`. Per boundaries, I did not reindex either graph.

